From dfc5bcc7824a4b65c766b08ae98a69947b1fdb2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: u <u@localhost>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:11:58 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 24/27] arm64: ole2disp: 16-bit VARIANT, SAFEARRAY and Invoke
 fixes

- Float arguments of VarUI1FromR4/VarBstrFromR4 arrive as 'long' in
  the 16-bit spec; add _conv entry points that reinterpret the bits
  (an ARM64 float would be expected in s0).
- SAFEARRAY16 element sizes are 16-bit sizes (SEGPTR, VARIANT16).
- Pass flat pointers where flat pointers are expected (VarXxxFromStr16,
  BstrFromVector16, SafeArrayCopy16, VectorFromBstr16 memcpy).
- DispCallFunc16: read the 16-bit vtable as SEGPTRs, pass the result
  pointer as a 16:16 pointer, use the WOWCallback16Ex based
  call_method on ARM64 too.
- ITypeInfo_fnInvoke16: keep the argument pointer array 32-bit side
  sized, map BYREF arguments with MapLS, use the 16-bit VARIANT
  helpers on VARIANT16.
- Convert FUNCDESC oVft between native and 16:16 vtable units.
- RegisterTypeLib: match the SDK prototype, fix the help directory
  (was a SEGPTR used as a pointer and strrchr(NULL)).
- CRITICAL_SECTION_DEBUG names do not fit the DWORD field on _WIN64.
- Include oleauto.h before wine/debug.h for wine_dbgstr_vt().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
